        {
          "id": "6996d2ab039e66ade3758576",
          "question": "<p>A coin is tossed three times. Find the probability of&nbsp;getting at least two heads.</p>",
          "image_url": null,
          "images": [],
          "type": "mcq",
          "options": [
            "<p>\\( \\frac{3}{8} \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( \\frac{1}{2} \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( \\frac{5}{8} \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( \\frac{7}{8} \\)</p>"
          ],
          "correct": 1,
          "explanation": "<p>Sample space,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>{</mo><mi>HHH</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>HHT</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>HTH</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>THH</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>TTT</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>TTH</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>THT</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>HTT</mi><mo>}</mo></math><br />Outcomes favourable to event 'at least two heads' are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HHH</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>HHT</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>HTH</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>THH</mi></math>.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mtext>at&#160;least&#160;two&#160;heads</mtext><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p>"
        },
        {
          "id": "6996d2ab039e66ade3758583",
          "question": "<p>Find the probability that a leap year will have 53, Fridays or 53 Saturdays.</p>",
          "image_url": null,
          "images": [],
          "type": "mcq",
          "options": [
            "<p>&nbsp;\\( \\frac{2}{7} \\)</p>",
            "<p>&nbsp;\\( \\frac{4}{7} \\)</p>",
            "<p>&nbsp;\\( \\frac{3}{7} \\)</p>",
            "<p>&nbsp;\\( \\frac{1}{7} \\)</p>"
          ],
          "correct": 2,
          "explanation": "<p>A leap year has 366 days. This is exactly 52 full weeks plus two extra days (\\(366=52\\times 7+2\\)). These two extra days determine if any specific day of the week appears a 53rd time.</p>\n<p>The two extra days must be consecutive. There are 7 possible, equally likely pairs for these consecutive days:&nbsp;<br />(Sunday, Monday)<br />(Monday, Tuesday)<br />(Tuesday, Wednesday)<br />(Wednesday, Thursday)<br />(Thursday, Friday)<br />(Friday, Saturday)<br />(Saturday, Sunday)</p>\n<p>We want the probability of having 53 Fridays (Event F) or 53 Saturdays (Event S).</p>\n<p>Event F (53 Fridays) occurs in pairs (Thursday, Friday) and (Friday, Saturday). \\(P(F)=\\frac{2}{7}\\).</p>\n<p>Event S (53 Saturdays) occurs in pairs (Friday, Saturday) and (Saturday, Sunday).</p>\n<p>\\(P(S)=\\frac{2}{7}\\).</p>\n<p>The event \\(F\\cap S\\) (both 53 Fridays and 53 Saturdays) occurs only with the pair (Friday, Saturday).</p>\n<p>\\(P(F\\cap S)=\\frac{1}{7}\\).</p>\n<p>Using the principle of inclusion-exclusion, the probability of the union is:</p>\n<p>\\(P(F\\cup S)=P(F)+P(S)-P(F\\cap S)=\\frac{2}{7}+\\frac{2}{7}-\\frac{1}{7}=\\frac{3}{7}\\)</p>"
        },
        {
          "id": "6996d2ab039e66ade3758580",
          "question": "<p>If \\( E \\) be any event and \\( P(E)=\\frac{2}{7} \\) the find odds in&nbsp;favour of \\( E \\)</p>",
          "image_url": null,
          "images": [],
          "type": "mcq",
          "options": [
            "<p>\\( \\frac{5}{2} \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( \\frac{2}{5} \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( \\frac{5}{7} \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( \\frac{7}{5} \\)</p>"
          ],
          "correct": 1,
          "explanation": "<p>let an event A, If Probability of occurring of A be P(A) and not occurring of A be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>'</mo></msup></mfenced></math>.<br />- Odds in favour of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>(</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&macr;</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac></math><br />- Odds in Against of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>(</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&macr;</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac></math></p>\n<p>If \\( E \\) be any event and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></math> then&nbsp;</p>\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></math></p>\n<p>odds in favour of \\( E \\)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math></p>"
        },
        {
          "id": "6996d2ab039e66ade3758570",
          "question": "<p>Let \\( A=\\{1,3,5,7,9\\} \\) and \\( B=\\{2,4,6,8\\} \\). If in a</p>\n<p>cartesian product \\( A \\times B,(a, b) \\) is chosen at random,then the probability of \\( a+b=9 \\) is</p>",
          "image_url": null,
          "images": [],
          "type": "mcq",
          "options": [
            "<p>\\( 1 / 4 \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( 1 / 5 \\)</p>",
            "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math></p>",
            "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math></p>"
          ],
          "correct": 1,
          "explanation": "<p>As <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></math>, therefore, total number of possible outcomes are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>.</mo></math> The ordered pairs&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>)</mo></math> such that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math> are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math>.&nbsp;<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>20</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math></p>"
        },
