          "type": "mcq",
          "options": [
            "<p>\\( \\frac{1}{11} \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( \\frac{2}{11} \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( \\frac{3}{11} \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( \\frac{6}{11} \\)</p>"
          ],
          "correct": 3,
          "explanation": "<p>Given, events A, B and C are mutually exclusive<br />and exhaustive, hence P (A&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8746;</mo></math> B&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8746;</mo></math> C) = 1</p>\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p>\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>11</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p>\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mn>11</mn></mfrac></math></p>"
